---
layout: none
# JSON with front matter (not .md) follows repo's search.json pattern;
# .md extension triggers Jekyll Markdown processing that wraps output in <p> tags.
#
# WHY THIS IS WRITTEN OUT BY HAND INSTEAD OF `courses | jsonify`
#
# It used to be exactly that one filter. It stopped being enough when price,
# credit points and the limited-seats flag became structured data in
# trainings.yml instead of hand-written German sentences: four consumer sites
# read `pricing`, `credits` and `few_seats` as STRINGS and render them
# verbatim, and jsonify would have silently changed their types.
#
# ADR-0004 says the feed is a contract, and CLAUDE.md spells out the rule:
# adding optional fields is free, changing an existing one is not. So every
# document below carries BOTH:
#
#   legacy (unchanged type, unchanged name)   new (structured)
#   ---------------------------------------   -----------------------------
#   pricing   "Frühbucherpreis ... 2.690 €"    price       { amount, currency,
#   credits   "20 methodische und 10 ..."                    early_bird }
#   few_seats "only few seats available"       credit_points { methodical, ... }
#                                              seats_limited true
#
# No published key ever changes type, so no consumer has to do anything, ever.
# The legacy strings are now GENERATED rather than stored, which is the whole
# point: `pricing` is rendered through _includes/price-label.html against the
# build date, so an expired early-bird offer stops being published on its own.
# Consumers that migrate to `price` get to render it in their own language;
# consumers that never migrate simply stop being lied to.
#
# The legacy strings are German, because that is what they have always been.
# Their exact money formatting changed once, at the migration, from "€ 2690"
# to "2.690 €" (correct German). That is cosmetic, not a type change.
---
{%- assign courses = site.data.trainings.courses -%}
{%- assign today = 'now' | date: '%Y-%m-%d' -%}
{
  "$schema": "https://trainings.arc42.org/api/trainings.schema.json",
  "generated": {{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema | jsonify }},
  "courses": [
{%- for course in courses %}
  {%- capture creditstr -%}{% include credits-label.html credits=course.credit_points lang="de" %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign creditstr = creditstr | strip -%}
    {
      {% if course.blurb %}"blurb": {{ course.blurb | strip | jsonify }},
      {% endif %}{% if course.certification %}"certification": {{ course.certification | jsonify }},
      {% endif %}{% if creditstr != "" %}"credits": {{ creditstr | append: " Punkte" | jsonify }},
      "credit_points": {{ course.credit_points | jsonify }},
      {% endif %}{% if course.url_en %}"url_en": {{ course.url_en | jsonify }},
      {% endif %}"id": {{ course.id | jsonify }},
      "short_title": {{ course.short_title | jsonify }},
      "title": {{ course.title | jsonify }},
      "url": {{ course.url | jsonify }},
      "trainers": {{ course.trainers | jsonify }},
      "dates": [
{%- for d in course.dates %}
  {%- capture pricestr -%}{% include price-label.html price=d.price lang="de" %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign pricestr = pricestr | strip -%}
        {
          {% if d.city %}"city": {{ d.city | jsonify }},
          {% endif %}{% if d.country %}"country": {{ d.country | jsonify }},
          {% endif %}{% if d.trainers %}"trainers": {{ d.trainers | jsonify }},
          {% endif %}{% if pricestr != "" %}"pricing": {{ pricestr | jsonify }},
          {%- comment -%}
            price is written out rather than jsonified so that an EXPIRED
            early_bird is omitted here too. Leaving it in would push the
            expiry decision onto four consumers, which is the arrangement
            this whole change exists to remove: the producer decides once,
            at build time, and everyone downstream can render what they get
            without a calendar.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          "price": {
            "amount": {{ d.price.amount }},
            "currency": {{ d.price.currency | default: "EUR" | jsonify }}{% if d.price.alumni %},
            "alumni": {{ d.price.alumni }}{% endif %}{% if d.price.early_bird.until >= today %},
            "early_bird": { "amount": {{ d.price.early_bird.amount }}, "until": {{ d.price.early_bird.until | jsonify }} }{% endif %}
          },
          {% endif %}{% if d.seats_limited %}"few_seats": "only few seats available",
          "seats_limited": true,
          {% endif %}"id": {{ d.id | jsonify }},
          "code": {{ d.code | jsonify }},
          "start": {{ d.start | jsonify }},
          "end": {{ d.end | jsonify }},
          "language": {{ d.language | jsonify }},
          "format": {{ d.format | jsonify }},
          "status": {{ d.status | jsonify }},
          "url": {{ d.url | jsonify }}
        }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{%- endfor %}
      ]
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{%- endfor %}
  ]
}
